/// \mainpage OpenLB API Reference
///
/// OpenLB is a C++ framework for lattice Boltzmann simulations, built around a
/// small set of composable pieces: a descriptor fixes the velocity set and the
/// fields a cell carries, dynamics decide how those cells collide, and a
/// lattice holds them and drives the time loop across CPUs and GPUs. This
/// reference documents those types as they appear in the source. For the
/// narrative introduction, the worked examples and the installation
/// instructions, see the <a href="../index.html">OpenLB User Guide</a>.
///
/// <ul>
/// <li><a href="topics.html">Topics</a> &mdash; the curated public interface,
///     grouped by subsystem. Start here.</li>
/// <li><a href="annotated.html">Classes</a> &mdash; every documented class and
///     struct, with its members and inheritance.</li>
/// <li><a href="concepts.html">Concepts</a> &mdash; the C++20 concepts that
///     constrain descriptors, dynamics and field types.</li>
/// <li><a href="namespaces.html">Namespaces</a> &mdash; the complete symbol
///     index, including free functions that belong to no class.</li>
/// <li><a href="files.html">Files</a> &mdash; the header tree, for when you
///     know where something lives but not what it is called.</li>
/// </ul>

/// \defgroup api OpenLB API
/// The curated public interface of OpenLB. Everything reachable from here is
/// meant to be used directly by application code.

/// \defgroup core Core
/// \ingroup api
/// Lattice data structures and the unit conversion between lattice and
/// physical quantities.

/// \defgroup descriptor Descriptors
/// \ingroup api
/// Compile-time description of a lattice: its dimension, velocity set and the
/// fields each cell carries.
